F1 src/windows/MainApp.tsx
cx simple
goal Add an "author" GroupMode to the PR rail so PRs can be grouped by author login, reusing existing sort/priority weighting and collapse-state logic.
bug y | MainApp.tsx:78 declares `type GroupMode = "org" | "repo" | "reason" | "type"` and the group-by `<select>` at lines 2021-2024 only offers org/repo/type/reason options — no author mode exists; the grouping key/label switch at lines 1692-1698 has no author branch either.
skip research,requirements,design
why This is a single-file, well-localized addition to an existing enum-driven grouping mechanism. All the pieces to reuse (authorPrioOf, PRIORITY_WEIGHT, groupPull, SORTERS, collapse-key namespacing) already exist and were confirmed by reading MainApp.tsx lines 1650-1735 and 2140-2192 — no new architecture, IPC, or settings needed. Classified simple: skip research/requirements/design but keep planning (to sequence the 4 small edits: type union, select option, key/label branch, header badge) and review (to verify sort/collapse behavior matches spec) since correctness of tie-breaking and priority badge placement matters.
files F1
